course: dictionary
lesson: 10715
title: Unused: not being used
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «unused» means not used, never used, or not being used right now. Look for the clues around it. «An unused notebook» has clean empty pages, because nobody has written in it yet.
explain: Unused has a second meaning with «to». «Unused to» means not familiar with something, not used to it. Say «unused» with a z sound (un-YOOZD) for the first meaning, and with an s sound (un-YOOST) for «unused to».
explain: «In the big boat-house all the fine boats hang up unused, and the place feels deserted.» The boats are not being used, and the clue deserted tells you nobody is there. Ask yourself: if I swap in "not used," does the sentence still make sense? It does.
fact: Unused means not used, never used, or not being used now.
fact: «Unused to» means not familiar with something, as in «unused to the cold».
fact: In «unused to», the word is said un-YOOST, not un-YOOZD.
fact: «An unused room» is a room that nobody is using at the moment.
fact: Unused food, paper or items can be saved, reused or given away.
exercise: «An unused notebook» has clean pages. What does unused mean here? | Full of writing | Lost and found | *Never used | Very old and worn
exercise: «Maya is unused to the cold.» What does unused to mean? | Freezing and frozen | Cold and wet | Very keen on cold weather | *Not used to it, not familiar with it
exercise: «All the fine boats hang up unused, and the place feels deserted.» What does unused tell you about the boats? | The boats are brand new and shiny | The boats are being used very hard | *They are not being used | The boats are sinking
test: «Shops may take back unused things, even if you just changed your mind.» What does unused mean in that line? | Used a lot | Stolen | *Not used, still in good condition | Broken
test: Which meaning fits «leave unused»? | *Leave something and do not use it | Give away a broken one | Leave in a hurry | Use it all up
exam: Which sentence uses «unused» to mean not familiar with something? | «The unused tickets were thrown away.» | «An unused room sat empty all winter.» | *«Tom is unused to city noise.» | «The unused paper was saved for art.»
